+*   **Strengths:** Eliminates the need for expensive runtime normal calculations [S1, unofficial]. Enhances interactivity for rotating datasets [S1, unofficial]. Effectively utilizes the CUDA memory hierarchy [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations:** Introduces a slight decrease in image correctness during rotation, though described as negligible [S1, unofficial]. Requires CPU preprocessing [S1, unofficial]. The choice of thread block dimensions affects performance and quality [S1, unofficial].
 *   **When to Use:** Interactive volume rendering of large datasets where iso-surface normals change frequently, and precomputation is acceptable [S1, unofficial].
 *   **When Not to Use:** Real-time applications where preprocessing time is prohibitive, or datasets with very low variance where fixed-step methods are sufficient [S1, unofficial].
